# Session handover notes — if you keep a local scratch file for in-progress
# work that isn't ready to share yet, ignore it here rather than committing it.
TASK-HANDOVER.md

# Personal Claude Code permission overrides — machine-specific, never shared.
# Without this, anyone's settings.local.json (which can carry broad personal
# grants, e.g. a whole-drive Read allowance) would get committed into this
# shared vault for every user to inherit.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Obsidian Local REST API plugin — holds the live API key + self-signed cert.
# Never commit this: it's the credential that lets anything on the machine
# read and write the vault over HTTP.
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# Installed community plugin code — reinstallable via Community plugins > Browse,
# not vault content. community-plugins.json (which plugins are enabled) is still tracked.
.obsidian/plugins/*/main.js
.obsidian/plugins/*/manifest.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/styles.css

# Local workspace/layout state — machine-specific, not shared config
.obsidian/workspace*.json

# Wiki-publish staging output (see docs/publishing-to-a-wiki.md) — regenerated by CI
.wiki-stage/

# Some tools default to saving output wherever the current working directory
# happens to be. If you notice a folder like this accumulating output that
# isn't actually vault content, ignore it here rather than committing it.
# e.g.:
# Claude outputs/

# --- Common patterns below; trim or extend for your stack ---

# Node artifact files
node_modules/
dist/

# Compiled Python bytecode
*.py[cod]

# Log files
*.log

# JetBrains IDE
.idea/

# Generated by MacOS
.DS_Store

# Generated by Windows
Thumbs.db

# Large media files
*.mp4
*.tiff
*.avi
*.flv
*.mov
*.wmv
